(6698352, 999197, 85430, '<td valign="top">The intensity of your expression is a winner here. People normally try to put on a smiling face when they have their portraits taken, but that only makes the image less memorable. Portraits that capture emotions, rather than faces, in my book, holds more value than the other. Well done on that aspect.  <br/> <br/>But i must say, the PP may be a little too much, specially it''s a male skin. The choice of high key may also be uncalled for, but no worries, i don''t think they hold much weight on the vote.<br/> <br/>7 from me.</td>', 'The intensity of your expression is a winner here. People normally try to put on a smiling face when they have their portraits taken, but that only makes the image less memorable. Portraits that capture emotions, rather than faces, in my book, holds more value than the other. Well done on that aspect.   But i must say, the PP may be a little too much, specially it''s a male skin. The choice of high key may also be uncalled for, but no worries, i don''t think they hold much weight on the vote. 7 from me.', '2012-03-02 13:44:46.000000', NULL, 1),
