(6703289, 1001679, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Fantastic composition, presentation and coloration - I normally have a real downer on object-based photographs (often a reflexive 1) and those with religious motifs. But I do like this. The symbology, the simplicity and the flat out confidence are all compelling.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not really.<br/> <br/>Overall: I''m pleased to be surprised that I like this.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Fantastic composition, presentation and coloration - I normally have a real downer on object-based photographs (often a reflexive 1) and those with religious motifs. But I do like this. The symbology, the simplicity and the flat out confidence are all compelling. Critical stuff: Not really. Overall: I''m pleased to be surprised that I like this.', '2012-03-07 18:03:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6703290, 1001494, 97225, '<td valign="top">Fabulous shot!</td>', 'Fabulous shot!', '2012-03-07 18:04:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6703295, 1000987, 97225, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!</td>', 'Beautiful!', '2012-03-07 18:07:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6703296, 1001166, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I know this is yours Ben but I''m not going to let that stop me from commenting and scoring. I feel like this is a photo within a photo - the man sat peacefully in the chair, perhaps enjoying the light - that whole quadrant of the image self contained... then we move our eye outwards and the context changes - the darkness has us and the figure on the right take on an ominous presence suggestive of endangerment of the peaceful guy. It''s like we''re seeing something we shouldn''t - a glimpse of a dark sub-strata of life that normally live at the periphery (even blind spot) of or perception and vision.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nope<br/> <br/>Overall: Perfectly judged.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I know this is yours Ben but I''m not going to let that stop me from commenting and scoring. I feel like this is a photo within a photo - the man sat peacefully in the chair, perhaps enjoying the light - that whole quadrant of the image self contained... then we move our eye outwards and the context changes - the darkness has us and the figure on the right take on an ominous presence suggestive of endangerment of the peaceful guy. It''s like we''re seeing something we shouldn''t - a glimpse of a dark sub-strata of life that normally live at the periphery (even blind spot) of or perception and vision. Critical stuff: Nope Overall: Perfectly judged.', '2012-03-07 18:08:39.000000', NULL, 1),
