(6704429, 999847, 54446, '<td valign="top">Wonderful light throughout the frame.  Nothing easy about controlling exposure in shadows and highlights in this situation.  Bravo!  That''s a beautiful aspen grove.  Amazing detail.  Great presentation and technique.  Well deserved top 10%.  Congrats!</td>', 'Wonderful light throughout the frame.  Nothing easy about controlling exposure in shadows and highlights in this situation.  Bravo!  That''s a beautiful aspen grove.  Amazing detail.  Great presentation and technique.  Well deserved top 10%.  Congrats!', '2012-03-08 15:12:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6704437, 1001520, 86799, '<td valign="top">Thanks, folks, for the kind comments.  This really did way better than I expected.  It''s been a long time coming to get one in the top 10.<br/> <br/>This was a salvage shot - I went down to that small lake to try to take a few shots of the power plant through the trees and fog.  The water was very high from a heavy storm the day before, so the access to the edge of the lake was set back about 20 feet.  I couldn''t get down far enough to even glimpse the stacks.  But the scene was quite peaceful and the light filtering through the low fog was soft and gentle.  The fog was pretty low...just over the trees...and with no wind the water surface was very steady.  I only stayed about 10 minutes, took about 15 shots, and this was the first of the batch.  It is quite serene and "zen", isn''t it?</td>', 'Thanks, folks, for the kind comments.  This really did way better than I expected.  It''s been a long time coming to get one in the top 10. This was a salvage shot - I went down to that small lake to try to take a few shots of the power plant through the trees and fog.  The water was very high from a heavy storm the day before, so the access to the edge of the lake was set back about 20 feet.  I couldn''t get down far enough to even glimpse the stacks.  But the scene was quite peaceful and the light filtering through the low fog was soft and gentle.  The fog was pretty low...just over the trees...and with no wind the water surface was very steady.  I only stayed about 10 minutes, took about 15 shots, and this was the first of the batch.  It is quite serene and "zen", isn''t it?', '2012-03-08 15:28:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6704440, 1001026, 30214, '<td valign="top">those rings really make the shot. Well done, congratulations!</td>', 'those rings really make the shot. Well done, congratulations!', '2012-03-08 15:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
